# Full pure-ramp (no-heater) sweep -- see CLAUDE.md's "Pure-ramp
# (no-heater) sweep" section. Same 801-ratio ratios.txt as the heater
# sweep (0.7-1.5 @ 0.001, same 900/250 runaway_tmax split) -- ratio/
# label/threshold selection doesn't depend on the heater at all, so this
# intentionally reuses that file rather than duplicating it.
#
# Promoted from sweep_noheater_smoketest.sub after the smoketest (14
# ratios, concentrated at the 0.90-0.911 boundary) came back clean: all
# three boundary ratios showed FLAT-TO-DECREASING dTmax/dt across the
# post-ramp hold window (not accelerating), total rise ~0.006-0.007K over
# the full 1.5s window -- no sign any of them were "on the verge" and
# just needed more time. Unchanged tEnd/observation window carried
# forward as-is; see CLAUDE.md for the full smoketest writeup.
#
# --heater-power 0 / --base-dir runs_noheater / noheater_$(label) as the
# actual --label: belt-and-suspenders against colliding with the heater
# dataset's identically-ratio'd runs/<label> directories once copied back.
#
# IMPORTANT Condor gotcha (found live -- the first version of this file
# only prefixed transfer_output_files, not the label passed to
# run_transient.py, and every job held on an output-transfer error):
# transfer_output_files returns only the BASENAME of whatever path you
# give it to the submit directory -- it does NOT preserve the leading
# work/runs_noheater/ structure. So this has ALWAYS landed as flat
# condor/<label>/ directories (sweep.sub's work/runs/$(label) included),
# never nested under runs/. That was invisible for the heater sweep
# (nothing else to collide with); it becomes a real collision risk the
# moment a second sweep reuses the same labels. Fix: the label itself
# must be unique BEFORE run_transient.py ever creates the directory --
# prefixing only the transfer path (without also changing `arguments`)
# just means Condor goes looking for a prefixed directory that was never
# actually created. The actual execute-side directory is
# work/<base-dir>/<whatever --label was>, full stop -- transfer_output_files
# must name that exact path, nothing else.

universe        = container
container_image = docker://ghcr.io/rosepowers29/local-freefem-electrothermal@sha256:8b39db74c15d90180fb623cda03211d434ce619cd3786c3abbd37de930aed37c
requirements = (Arch == "X86_64")

executable      = condor_run_ratio.sh
arguments       = $(ratio) noheater_$(label) --ramp-rate 20 --ramp-dt 999 --runaway-tmax $(runaway_tmax) --heater-power 0 --base-dir runs_noheater

should_transfer_files   = YES
when_to_transfer_output = ON_EXIT
transfer_input_files    = payload.tar.gz
transfer_output_files   = work/runs_noheater/noheater_$(label)

request_cpus   = 1
request_memory = 4096M
request_disk   = 2048M

output = logs/noheater_$(label).out
error  = logs/noheater_$(label).err
log    = logs/noheater_$(label).log
stream_output = True
stream_error  = True

# Same auto-retry policy as sweep.sub -- see its comments for the full
# rationale (node-heterogeneity, RETRY_WORTHY exit codes).
on_exit_hold        = (ExitCode != 0)
on_exit_hold_reason  = "run_transient.py reported a RETRY_WORTHY status (see CLAUDE.md) -- auto-releasing to retry, likely on a different execute node"
periodic_release     = (NumJobStarts < 4) && ((CurrentTime - EnteredCurrentStatus) > 300)

queue ratio,label,runaway_tmax from ratios_over.txt
